{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1469591-hiiden-way-to-gain-xp","id":1469591,"title":"Hiiden way to gain xp","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-04T14:22:51-08:00","id":1469591,"title":"Hiiden way to gain xp","content":"In the abyss realm of the umbra, a pack brave enough to travel here can gain xp by exloring. So if traveler can gain knowledge by visiting a realm of the umbra it could be possible through a forgotten rite or by some gameplay mechanics<br /> <br /> The reason i think about it is because my players are preparing for a big battle to protect their Cairn, but the problem is that they have not been able to get much outside help and are ill-prepared for battle because they have been upgrading their social skills in order to obtain food and technology resources. They want to improve their combat skills but have very little time to do so and risk losing their home, around 2 weeks maybe less. <br /> So they were planning to go in the abyss to gain more xp but that realm is hum... far too dangerous for them. So maybe by make them roll a special dice pool to gain xp from Cairn activities or search an old rite allowing them to access the wisdom and knowledge of their ancestors<br /> <br /> Maybe some of you have already invented a game mechanic that goes in this direction to get players out of a bad situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T17:38:11-08:00","id":1469603,"title":"","content":"Honestly? With the limited amount of time they are much better off using those already developed social skills to gather as many allies and alliances as possible, if they're willing to go deep in the hole for the next few years and have a Caern Totem with a modicum of sense they can gather a lot of spirit allies ( and possibly other Garou/Fera with an outside chance of other Night Folk) in a relatively short time..........chiminage is gonna be a bitch but thems the breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T10:07:11-08:00","id":1469652,"title":"","content":"Do not go through that rabbit hole, you have better options.<br /> <br /> If your players don't have any idea on how to improve their chances (acquiring allies, amassing fetishes, bringing in mundane military equipment or any other way to do it), you can provide them spiritual help. You, as the ST have the power to put spirits on their side, maybe due to some fate of them or the significance of this Caern to the spirits (spirits don't have to act on the same assumptions as werewolves do). You can even place a Tribal Totem or other Incarna to help their side.<br /> <br /> And if in the end you decide what they need is more xp <b><i>just give it to them</i></b>. Do not, under any circumstance, put in the players hands a tool to draw XP when they want, as adjusting the pace of growth in the game is your job.<br /> <br /> You don't have to follow the advice on the book for rewarding XP. Use anything you want, totem blessing, deep experiences, a dream journey to unlock hidden powers, whatever to justify, and then just give them as much XP as you deem necessary, it doesn't matter if it is two, three, forty times the usual amount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T10:21:26-08:00","id":1469653,"title":"","content":"You could just postpone the attack, you are the one who decide when it happens, just come up with something, anything as a reason for why the attack hasn't happen yet so that you can let your players get some xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T14:08:47-08:00","id":1469663,"title":"","content":"Or the attack can just not be as bad as the PCs think it's going to be. Relatively small mistakes on a command level can sabotage the effectiveness of a military raid in large ways.<br /> <br /> As noted, the ST has the power here. If your PCs aren't going to be up to the threat you were intending.... change the threat. You don't have to make it feel easy, but you can still tilt the odds in the players' favor without a drop of XP.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:21:24-08:00","id":1469669,"title":"","content":"Put a mechanics they could use anytime they want is a bad idea, yes, but one of them had an interesting idea:<br /> During their time in the Caern, as an ST i can submit to them some duty tasks: hunting for food, help teaching the young werewolves, assist in the performance of a ritual, smithing etc... those task would be asked when the ST think the moment is appropriate (in their case smithing for weapons, ritual to weaken the wyrm forces, calling spirits...) each task will require a certain amount of time and depending on their complexity and if the player has the ability to do them, he will have a certain amount of xp<br /> Hunting would take a day and would give 1 xp while forging tools and weapons would take several days and would give 2 or 3 xp.<br /> Again those task would be asked ingame only if the ST declare it or if the situation ask it. Hunting everyday or smithing for weeks without reason would not be very logic with the real needs of the Caern","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T15:59:46-08:00","id":1469674,"title":"","content":"This is still attaching too strict constraints on how they get XP and that's not how XP really works or what it represents.<br /> <br /> XP isn't a natural resource that exists in the setting and the PCs get through defined means. It is an abstraction for growth meant to be used by the Storyteller as a means to achieve three goals:<br /> <br /> 1- Control the pace of growth in the chronicle, so you know what to expect as time passes;<br /> <br /> 2- Reward whatever you consider adequate behavior, encouraging the players to act in certain ways;<br /> <br /> 3- Share responsibility with the players on their growth, so you give the points, they chose how to spend them.<br /> <br /> But that's all an Out-of-Character thing. XP isn't a narrative tool, it doesn't exist in the story, the characters don't have a concept for it or know it exists. It is <b>not</b> meant to be given following clear criteria. Those are just guides.<br /> <br /> Your situation is that you decided to throw at them a challenge that you think is beyond their current power level. This is your problem, not the way to give them more XP. How do you solve it?<br /> <br /> If you're not satisfied with other ways to solve it (give them more resources and allies, weaken or postpone the threat, or just play it as is and capture or let them escape, change the chronicle expectations to let the Caern fall) and you decide that it really is with their power level...<br /> <br /> Well, just do it. Stop rationalizing how they get XP and just give them XP. Do not attach extra XP to the little things they do during this time, just let them do things to actually improve the Caern and then give them more XP than usual. You don't need any reason to do so beyond 'I want to'.<br /> <br /> Another option is to give them the things they would buy with XP. Just give it directly. Have some totem teach them new Gifts, someone teach them skills, or even increase an Attribute rating. Cut the middle man and just let them know this is a one-time thing, not something they can count on in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T16:44:47-08:00","id":1469677,"title":"","content":"Also, something very specific to WtA?<br /> <br /> WtA has an in-narrative advancement resource: Renown. All those ideas of small things to do to help around the Sept? Those are all examples of minor temporary Renown awards in the books. Those are ways to earn some Renown during slow times, and thus earn the Respect needed to gain Rank and the privileges attached to it. Adding XP rewards to Renown rewards is a questionable decision by itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T08:29:36-08:00","id":1469738,"title":"","content":"Wait guys, the xp gain for a long and complex task would be maximum 5, in those 2 weeks they could earn only around 10 xp bonus not dozens.<br /> Plus they are still limited by the cost of the gifts and abilities, and the fact that according to the v20 book, their attributes and abilities are only upgradables by 1 per scenario. Finally i say it again, those task are not available all the time, only when the st say it's possible<br /> Some of them have saved their xp and have a few dozen in reserve, but others have spent them as they went along and have barely 3 or 5, so with these bonuses they would go up to a little more than 10, not enough to buy very powerful stuff but enough to invest in an extra dice in a dice pool.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the experience is not only a way to balance the gameplay but also represent what the character learn, and they can learn new things by making some special actions like Caern tasks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T11:00:04-08:00","id":1469750,"title":"","content":"OK, hold up.<br /> <br /> You have players sitting on piles of dozens of XP, and you're worried they don't have the stats to take on an upcoming threat... so you want to give them more XP?<br /> <br /> If they have reserves of dozens of XP, how is more going to solve anything?<br /> <br /> I mean, I have a whole post ready on why the &quot;XP for doing IC tasks&quot; is a bad thing logic there, but to keep to your own original stated issue, it seems like XP rates are not the main issue here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T11:37:09-08:00","id":1469754,"title":"","content":"I have to agree. It seems like you lost focus of your problem by focusing too much on your first idea of a solution.<br /> <br /> What do you intend for them? Why do you think they'll fail as they currently are? How did you arrived to the conclusion that XP would solve it? What do you expect them to do with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T13:21:39-08:00","id":1469761,"title":"","content":"Okay, read the thread and there are couple of questions that arose to me;<br /> <br /> 1. How much downtime/bluebooking do the players do? Sept tasks could be put in downtimes to justify raising abilities/learning gifts.<br /> <br /> 2. You started by saying that players had to raise their stats to earn food and technology. Are they not allowed to eat at the Caern or just buy technology using their resources background?<br /> <br /> 3. How tightly do you control their XP spending? Usually, XP hoarding is a sign the players don't feel they are justified enough to use the XP.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T15:22:38-08:00","id":1469771,"title":"","content":"Ok let me be more specific:<br /> I play the role of the ST with friends and therefore 5 PCs<br /> As I said they focused on social, 3 of them spent their xp as they went along to improve their social attributes and abilities. They arrived to high dice grouping in social but they invested very little in physical attributes and gifts<br /> The last 2, more used to rpg have respectively 16 and 20 xp (I asked them earlier to not say stupid things) in reserve and have invested in various gifts to &quot;adjust&quot; the conversations and negotiations to their advantages but they have few fighting gifts<br /> <br /> They have evolved together and have ranks ranging from 2 to 3 and one of them has just passed rank 4.<br /> <br /> Their group is specialized in negotiations with humans and kinfolk to support Caern and help the warriors to protect it while they serve as a pillar for the sept.<br /> <br /> They have taken in Kinfolk refugees who were driven from their homes by a Pentex subsidiary, but a spy slipped in and an attack was organized, but the players realized it too late. They sent some of their forces to deal with a group of Fomori but it turned out to be a diversion and the allies they sent are no longer heard from, and Caern is surrounded by Fomori camps led by a pack of Black spiral dancers who watch the physical world and the umbra. <br /> <br /> In this situation the Caern lacks warriors and all of them will have to fight, but they have very little real offensive power and will need more power to fight back and survive.<br /> <br /> As you already said as ST I can just give them xp or look for a narrative reason to help them overcome this ordeal. Or I can just let things happen and let them lose their home, which is also a nice continuation of the story with a new goal for the players: revenge<br /> <br /> But perhaps due to inexperience on my part, I'm not a fan of the idea of the ST saving the day because the story doesn't suit him and he's directly or indirectly helping the players. Instead, I prefer to give them the opportunity to retaliate even with small means but which are justified in the story. <br /> <br /> In this case with the limits of improvement of their characteristics those who have a lot of xp invested them in brawl or firearms and athleticism to defend themselves but they have very few dice to throw, so they try to fill their lack of power by buying combat gifts<br /> On the other hand, the 3 others who already have little xp can hardly buy anything to prepare themselves <br /> <br /> As a ST I don't want to save them but I don't want to let them down either, my goal is to give them the means to fight but with low chances, and to see if by thinking of a good strategy they will manage to save their home or on the contrary if they will fail. But just telling them &quot;here is a gift of 20 points of xp each&quot; or &quot;a spirit comes and teaches you several powers for free&quot; or &quot;your lost allies are alive and they come back with reinforcements (found we don't know where) and the battle turns to your advantage&quot;... for me it takes away the tension in the game because the players can tell themselves that the ST will save them if they have problems.<br /> <br /> But you're probably right, maybe i focus on the wrong side of the problem, I have less than a year of experience as an ST so I make a lot of rookie mistakes x)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 12-06-2021, 06:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T16:57:41-08:00","id":1469786,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Talk to them. See what they want.<br /> <br /> You don't have to tell them everything of course. But be honest, tell them you feel like you've guided them into a corner, and you're not sure how to get out of it in a way that they'll enjoy. Maybe they'll be OK with some deus ex machina to make it through the situation. Players do understand that a new ST is learning and sometimes mistakes take correcting in hard to hide ways. Maybe they're OK with doing the best they can with what they've got, and if it goes belly up, so be it.<br /> <br /> You can do this for decades and still find yourself in a bind. The vast majority of players I've ever gamed with appreciate being asked about how to deal with such binds (it helps maintain agency even if the game is going to be low agency for a bit to undo the bind). I've never had a player get nasty with me for asking their opinion on things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-06T22:48:39-08:00","id":1469805,"title":"","content":"I've talk to them and the majority think more xp is the solution, that's why i came here to ask, but i'll just talk more to them and we'll find a solution everyone will be ok with","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T00:43:55-08:00","id":1469809,"title":"","content":"I'll admit to being very confused that this group with massive social clout haven't managed to amass a network of contacts, allies and alliances....it seems exactly what they are built for.<br /> <br /> Hell, get them to talk various spirits into giving them one off boons for this particular battle with their awesome social skills; this will not be 'free' but will involve large amounts of chiminage which can propel various storylines in your chronicle for decades to come. That way they are still punching above their current weight but you don't have the issue of artificially inflated tanks to deal with for the rest of the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T00:52:20-08:00","id":1469810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1469591-hiiden-way-to-gain-xp?p=1469809#post1469809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit to being very confused that this group with massive social clout haven't managed to amass a network of contacts, allies and alliances....it seems exactly what they are built for.<br /> <br /> Hell, get them to talk various spirits into giving them one off boons for this particular battle with their awesome social skills; this will not be 'free' but will involve large amounts of chiminage which can propel various storylines in your chronicle for decades to come. That way they are still punching above their current weight but you don't have the issue of artificially inflated tanks to deal with for the rest of the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this would be a great thing to show the result of their build skills/duties.<br /> <br /> And, once more, downtime is there to add to these allies.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T03:17:30-08:00","id":1469816,"title":"","content":"I too think them talking to the spirits for that little extra in exchange for future favors would help things, but the crux of the matter lies in a single point:<br /> <br /> You don't want to interfere, but you also don't want to let them get what will come. Those are contradicting goals.<br /> <br /> One thing about talking to your players: the goal is not to just ask them what they think the solution is. It is to consult them about what they think of the solutions you have. The players don't have reason to answer anything beyond &quot;more XP&quot; because this is the only solution they have direct agency over and direct contact with, unless some of them are far more experienced than you as a Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Another two points to make clear: your interference doesn't have to make things easy, just easier, enough for your tastes; and sudden interference from the outside doesn't have to be without cost.<br /> <br /> For example, you could put a band of Ronin stalking those enemies and be able to lend help, but they'll ask for acceptance in the Sept and help to be accept by a tribe or even to get Gifts and stuff while remaining Ronin. Your players will be on a tight spot if they accept such help. Or the help could come from hunters or other supernatural group with their own agenda, and the players have to deal with those later.<br /> <br /> But if you stick to the idea that XP is the solution, go for it. It is too abstract to worry about not making sense. You can have a dream quest that takes forever in a non-time place, revisit past achievements, have a totem bless them, or just decide that the present pressure and stress for sheer survival is driving them to take more from each lesson life teaches them.<br /> <br /> Giving XP isn't the only solution, but if you decide it is your solution do not put yourself in a corner by denying yourself of your own decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}